  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02MQ">Lemma <span data-tag="02MQ">12.10.4</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$, $\mathcal{B}$ be abelian categories. Let $F : \mathcal{A} \to \mathcal{B}$ be an exact functor. Then the full subcategory of objects $C$ of $\mathcal{A}$ such that $F(C) = 0$ forms a Serre subcategory of $\mathcal{A}$. </p>
